content:
SupportBot: New escalation opened from account acct_9XH3 — customer reports streaming tool-call args being truncated mid-JSON, causing schema validation failures and downstream tool errors. Priority: P2.

Sam W: forwarding the customer transcript and repro steps here. they hit this in production when using the streaming endpoint with function/tool calling. requests succeed in non-stream mode.

Sam W: summary of observed failure: model emits a tool_call with arguments split across streaming frames. the final closing brace sometimes arrives in a later chunk or never (connection dropped). our SDK tries to validate the JSON as each chunk arrives and fails with parse error. customer sees: "400 Bad Request - invalid_tool_args".

Maria P: can you paste the raw stream (captured) or the HTTP body chunks? also need sdk version, model, and any gateway logs.

Sam W: pasted below (redacted account + timestamps). note: the stream was captured server-side before our app-layer aggregator.

Luca T: here is the relevant portion of the server capture (we've abbreviated other unrelated frames):

```
data: {"id":"msg-1","type":"message","role":"assistant","tool_call":{"name":"get_user_profile","arguments":"{\"user_id\":\"12345\",\"fields\":[\"email\",\"profile\"],\"include_inactive\":false"}}
data: {"id":"msg-2","type":"message","role":"assistant","tool_call":{"name":"get_user_profile","arguments":"}

```

Luca T: second chunk only contains the trailing characters for the JSON (`}"`) and sometimes the connection closes before that arrives. in this capture the second chunk is actually just `}"` on its own line but earlier we saw cases where the trailing `}` never arrived.

Maria P: thanks. that matches the schema validation error: our parser tries to JSON.parse the arguments string when the first chunk arrives and fails because it's not closed. two immediate asks: (1) can you reproduce reliably with a minimal curl or SDK script? (2) what's the client behavior on partial args (are you passing through chunks to a consumer that expects full JSON)?

Luca T: repro script attached (short):

```
# curl style skeleton (customer)
curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" \
  -d '{"model":"gpt-4o-stream","stream":true,"function_calls":"auto","functions":[{"name":"get_user_profile","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"user_id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["user_id"]}}]}' \
  https://api.redwood-inference.example/v1/chat/stream
```

Luca T: SDK version: 0.9.2, gateway region: us-west-2, model: gpt-4o-stream-2025-10, observed around 2025-12-08 17:12:34 UTC.

Niya K: quick triage notes:
- reproduces locally with 0.9.2 when streaming directly and piping chunks to a naive JSON parser.
- does NOT reproduce with non-stream (stream:false) or with latest internal dev build 0.10.0-dev where we coalesce tool_call fragments before emitting.
- probable root cause: streaming gateway emits incremental tokens as they are produced by the model. our client-side helper previously assumed tool_call.arguments would be emitted as a single contiguous frame; it did not implement brace/quote balancing.

Maria P: mitigation options for customer (short term):
1) switch to non-streaming calls for tool-heavy flows.
2) buffer incoming stream frames until you detect a balanced JSON (simple algorithm: count open/close braces outside quotes, ignore escaped quotes).
3) upgrade to SDK >=0.10.0 when available (contains coalescing fix and safer parser).

Sam W: customer asked about a server-side workaround so they don't have to change code. can infra gate a fix?

Infra Bot: pinging eng-runtime and eng-infra. suggested patch: coalesce contiguous tool_call.arguments tokens at the gateway level and only emit message events for tool_call once the arguments are syntactically balanced OR a configurable timeout elapses. this will be a small change in stream assembly. logging and metrics needed to ensure we don't increase latency for small tokens.

Maria P: next steps for support:
- (Sam) propose the buffering workaround to customer and offer a temporary client-side snippet (we'll paste below).
- (Niya) coordinate with eng-runtime to prioritize a coalescing patch (target: next minor patch, estimated ETA 3 business days).
- (Support Tier2) create incident and link to support ticket INC-2025-4789. assign to eng-runtime if infra change required.

Support Tier2: created INC-2025-4789, routed to eng-runtime. attaching customer transcript and repro script.

Sam W: sending the recommended client snippet to the customer now. snippet (JS) to accumulate and parse safely: 

```
// naive balance-based collector
let buffer = '';
function onChunk(chunk) {
  buffer += chunk;
  // attempt to extract tool_call.arguments string if present
  const match = /"tool_call"\s*:\s*\{[\s\S]*?"arguments"\s*:\s*"([\s\S]*)$/m.exec(buffer);
  if (match) {
    // match[1] is remainder of args string start; only try to parse when braces balanced
    if (isBracesBalanced(match[1])) {
      const argStr = match[1].replace(/\\\"/g, '"');
      try { const args = JSON.parse(argStr); handleToolCall(args); buffer = ''; } catch (e) { /* wait for more */ }
    }
  }
}

function isBracesBalanced(s) {
  let depth = 0; let inQuotes = false; let esc = false;
  for (let ch of s) {
    if (esc) { esc = false; continue; }
    if (ch === '\\') { esc = true; continue; }
    if (ch === '"') { inQuotes = !inQuotes; continue; }
    if (inQuotes) continue;
    if (ch === '{') depth++; if (ch === '}') depth--;
  }
  return depth <= 0 && !inQuotes;
}
```

Niya K: good. also control-plane change: add a flag to gateway to emit a `tool_call.partial` event when coalescing is in progress so clients can show a spinner instead of failing.

Sam W: customer responded: they can accept the client buffer but asked for a timeline to a server-side fix. I told them 3 business days and we'll provide daily updates.

Maria P: please keep this thread in sync with incident notes. i'll escalate priority if more customers report this.

Support Tier2: noted — adding a watch for similar support tickets (tag: stream-tool-args).

Luca T: thanks everyone. applying the buffer workaround now. I'll report back if anything else shows up. :thumbsup:

Sam W: marking action items: (1) send buffer snippet and link to ticket -> done. (2) eng-runtime patch -> Niya owns. (3) follow up to customer in 24h -> Sam.

Infra Bot: scheduled eng-runtime patch in sprint, PR link: internal/repo/eng-runtime/stream-coalesce#42 (internal).

Maria P: closing loop for now. will reopen if more symptoms surface.

Sam W: thanks all.
